WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
Picture two countries that start
out exactly as rich as each other.

2
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.970
In one, output per person
grows 2 percent a year.

3
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.250
In the other, 7 percent.

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:14.480
After 35 years, the first
is about 2 times as big.

5
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.220
The second is about 10.7 times as big.

6
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.960
So what drives growth?

7
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.770
Can an economy keep growing
just by people spending more?

8
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:28.070
In this mission, you'll calculate the
growth rate of real GDP per capita,

9
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.620
step by step.

10
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.670
Then you'll use a graph lab:

11
00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:35.860
move two sliders and watch
real GDP and the price level.

12
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.880
Your mission: figure out
what it really takes to keep

13
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.250
an economy growing year after year.
